unreleased
- added set_precision("single"/"double") for opt-in single precision (double stays the default)
- homogeneous material parameters are stored as O(1) copy-on-write expanded views;
  indexed writes (material["Ms"][domain] = ...) materialize them transparently, other
  in-place operations on a never-written homogeneous parameter now raise and require
  Material.materialize(key) first
- demag/Oersted/VectorPotential kernels are now always evaluated on the CPU in chunks
  (new chunk_cells option), which removes the large device memory spike during setup;
  values are unchanged (cached kernel files remain compatible)
- reduced allocations and GPU synchronization in LLGSolver, RKF45/56, MinimizerBB,
  SD_solver and Minimizer_LBFGS; constant ExternalField and ThermalField prefactors
  are cached; non-equidistant demag uses a batched einsum instead of a python loop
- fixed discarded nan_to_num results in LLGWithLESolver (the C==0 NaN guard was a no-op)
- fixed Minimizer_LBFGS tensor aliasing and hard-coded float64 scratch tensors
- ScalarLogger defaults to fsync_every=100 (rows are still flushed every write);
  FieldLogger no longer rewrites the whole .pvd document through minidom on every log
- added bench/ with GPU benchmark scripts and a vast.ai setup guide
- the field returned by a constant ExternalField.h() shares its storage between
  calls; an indexed write by the caller materializes a private copy (copy-on-write)
- kernel cache files written at a different floating point precision are cast on
  load (with a warning when this loses precision)
- DemagFieldPBC caches its spectral factors and uses rfftn (half-spectrum) instead
  of rebuilding all transfer functions and running a full complex fftn every call

